{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And you shall do no manner of work on this very day, for it is the Day of Atonement.</b> The reason Scripture here mentioned the language of atonement (כפרה) and the language of 'essence' (עצם) is so that you should not say: since no offering is mentioned in this passage, if there is no Sanctuary and no offering, then Yom ha-Kippurim does not atone — therefore it comes to say that the atonement does not depend on the offering or on anything else, but the essence of the day itself atones. It possesses this special quality, that it atones — provided one repents — in the manner that they expounded from the language of אך בעשור, and as I have mentioned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:54.279442321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}